Look, I'm tired of all this polymorph junk.  Why not do this:
Only allow the wand of polymorph to polymorph ONE item at a time
(on each pile in the range).
Is there any legitimate reason to polymorph a whole stack of items???
I'd like to blast away at a wand and hope it turns into wishing.
I strongly think that should be possible.  It's part of the fun.
This way, there's still some skill (learn to line up a row of items)
without the abuse potential.
It's simple, clean, and goes a long way to avoiding the major payoffs
while still allowing me to "get lucky" now and then.

If something more is still needed (I doubt it) give a 5% of destroying
the item (based on luck maybe) and let a polymorph demon (one of the coolest
ideas I've read so far) pop out and scramble you.

This would make the wand a much more valuable resource (you won't waste
it as easily) but doesn't have  hidden complexity.

